  "description": "YELRAL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H104 Dy11 N28 O68 1+,H1 O1 1-,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.629-3.974 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.74-117.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy11(ovpho)4(μ-CH3O)2(μ-H2O)2(μ3-OH)6(CH3OH)4(H2O)2(NO3)8](OH)·3CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
